# RLHF-style three-objective bandit on a stationary prompt distribution.
# Tests M=3 reward vectors (helpful, harmless, honest) — the canonical
# HH-RLHF objective decomposition. No distribution shift; this is the
# "ceiling" config that establishes how each algorithm handles M>2.

name: rlhf_helpful_harmless
description: |
  Stationary RLHF-style benchmark with three reward objectives
  (helpful, harmless, honest). Three prompt clusters with distinct
  arm-reward profiles per cluster. The test is whether algorithms
  can find the per-cluster Pareto front when M=3.

  To plug in real HH-RLHF / PKU-SafeRLHF data, set csv_path to a CSV
  with columns prompt_id, embedding_0..embedding_{d-1}, arm_id,
  helpful, harmless, honest. See examples/rlhf_dataset_prep.md.
horizon: 10000
n_seeds: 20
delta: 0.05

environment:
  type: RLHFBandit
  n_arms: 4
  embedding_dim: 4
  n_clusters: 3
  schedule: none
  sigma: 0.05

algorithms:
algorithms:
  - PCBShift
  - Auer16
  - ParetoUCB
  - AnnealingPareto
  - Kone23
  - Cai24
  - ScalarizedUCB
  - RandomPlay

metrics:
  - PreferenceRegret
  - HausdorffRegret
  - DominanceCoverage
  - ParetoPrecisionRecall
